LC - 560
// PATTERN: Prefix Sum + HashMap (Frequency Count)
// Problem: 560 - Subarray Sum Equals K
//
// IDEA:
// Agar index j tak ka prefix sum = S_j aur index i tak ka prefix sum = S_i (i < j),
// to subarray (i+1 ... j) ka sum = S_j - S_i.
// Hume ye sum k chahiye, yaani S_j - S_i = k  =>  S_i = S_j - k
// To har j pe bas ye dekhna hai: "pehle kitni baar prefix sum (S_j - k) aa chuka hai?"
// Har aisi baar ek valid subarray banta hai.

int subarraySum(vector<int>& nums, int k) {

    // key = prefix sum, value = ab tak ye prefix sum kitni baar aaya (FREQUENCY)
    // Frequency isliye store karte hain kyunki hume COUNT chahiye, longest nahi.
    // (525 mein longest chahiye tha, wahan sirf pehla index store hota hai.)
    unordered_map<int,int> mpp;

    int sum = 0;   // running prefix sum

    // Prefix sum 0 ek baar "already seen" maano (empty prefix).
    // Kyu? Agar shuru se hi koi subarray ka sum k ho (sum == k),
    // to diff = sum - k = 0 milna chahiye, warna wo subarray miss ho jayegi.
    mpp[0]++;

    int cnt = 0;   // valid subarrays ka total count

    for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {

        // Current element add karke prefix sum update karo
        sum += nums[i];

        // Hume aisa purana prefix chahiye jiska value (sum - k) ho,
        // taaki beech wale hisse ka sum exactly k aaye
        int diff = sum - k;

        // Agar diff pehle kabhi aaya hai, to utni hi subarrays
        // current index pe end ho rahi hain jinka sum k hai.
        // cnt mein += frequency (sirf +1 nahi), kyunki diff kai baar aa chuka ho sakta hai
        // (negative numbers ya zeros ki wajah se same prefix sum repeat ho sakta hai).
        if (mpp.find(diff) != mpp.end()) {
            cnt += mpp[diff];
        }

        // Current prefix sum ko map mein daalo, AFTER check karne ke.
        // Order important hai: pehle check, phir insert.
        // Warna k = 0 hone pe element khud ke saath match ho jayega (galat count).
        mpp[sum]++;
    }

    return cnt;
}

// Time: O(n)  (ek pass, HashMap ke operations average O(1))
// Space: O(n) (worst case har prefix sum alag ho)
//
// Sliding window yahan kyu nahi chalti? Kyunki nums mein negative numbers ho sakte hain,
// to window badhane/ghatane se sum monotonic nahi rehta. Prefix + HashMap negatives ke saath bhi chalta hai.


LC: 1074 (exact question but matrix implementation)

int numSubmatrixSumTarget(vector<vector<int>>& matrix, int target) {
    int rows = matrix.size();
    int cols = matrix[0].size();
    int count = 0;

    // STEP 1: Har row ka prefix sum banao (left se right).
    // Kyu? Taaki kisi bhi row mein "left se right tak ka sum" O(1) mein mil jaye.
    // Ab matrix[r][c] = us row mein column 0 se column c tak ka sum.
    for (int r = 0; r < rows; r++) {
        for (int c = 1; c < cols; c++) {
            matrix[r][c] += matrix[r][c - 1];
        }
    }

    // STEP 2: Left edge fix karo.
    // Kyu? Rectangle ki width define karne ke liye left aur right dono chahiye.
    for (int left = 0; left < cols; left++) {

        // STEP 3: Right edge fix karo (left se aage tak).
        // Kyu? Har possible width try karni hai: left..left, left..left+1, ... left..cols-1.
        // Ab (left, right) pair se width fix ho gayi.
        for (int right = left; right < cols; right++) {

            // Har (left, right) pair ke liye fresh start chahiye,
            // kyunki ye alag strip hai, isliye map aur sum yahin declare hote hain.
            int runningSum = 0;                  // top se current row tak strip ka total
            unordered_map<int, int> prefixCount; // prefix sum -> kitni baar aaya
            
            // Kyu 0 -> 1? "Kuch bhi row skip nahi ki" (top = row 0 se start)
            // wali rectangles ko count karne ke liye.
            prefixCount[0] = 1;

            // STEP 4: Upar se neeche traverse karo.
            // Current row = bottom edge. Ye height badalta hai.
            for (int bottom = 0; bottom < rows; bottom++) {

                // Is row mein left..right ka sum nikalo.
                // matrix[bottom][right] = column 0 se right tak
                runningSum += matrix[bottom][right];

                // Column 0 se left-1 tak ka hissa hatao,
                // taaki sirf left..right ka sum bache.
                if (left > 0) {
                    runningSum -= matrix[bottom][left - 1];
                }

                // STEP 5: 1D "Subarray Sum Equals K" trick.
                // Hume chahiye: koi purani top edge jahan se bottom tak sum == target ho.
                // Matlab: runningSum - oldPrefix == target
                //   => oldPrefix = runningSum - target
                int needed = runningSum - target;

                // Agar ye prefix pehle aaya tha, toh utni hi valid rectangles
                // is bottom pe khatam ho rahi hain (har purana prefix = ek alag top edge).
                if (prefixCount.find(needed) != prefixCount.end()) {
                    count += prefixCount[needed];
                }

                // Current prefix ko map mein daalo, aage ki rows ke liye
                // ye ek possible top edge ban jayega.
                prefixCount[runningSum]++;
            }
        }
    }

    return count;
}

LC : 525
// PATTERN: Balance / Equal-Count Prefix Sum
//          (Prefix Sum + HashMap storing FIRST index, with value transformation)
// Problem: 525 - Contiguous Array
//
// IDEA:
// "0 aur 1 ki barabar count" ko "sum = 0" mein badalna hai.
// Trick: 0 ko -1 maan lo, 1 ko +1 rehne do.
// Ab agar kisi subarray mein barabar 0 aur 1 hain, to +1 aur -1 cancel ho jayenge
// aur us subarray ka sum = 0 hoga.
//
// Sum 0 wala subarray kaise dhundhein?
// Agar index i pe prefix sum = X tha, aur baad mein index j pe bhi prefix sum = X hai,
// to beech ke hisse (i+1 ... j) ka sum = X - X = 0.
// Yaani "same prefix sum dobara dikha" = "beech ka subarray balanced hai".

int findMaxLength(vector<int>& nums) {

    int cumsum = 0;   // running balance (+1 for '1', -1 for '0')

    // key = balance, value = wo balance PEHLI BAAR kis index pe aaya
    unordered_map<int,int> mpp;

    // Empty prefix (index -1) pe balance 0 tha.
    // Kyu? Agar shuru se hi balance 0 ho jaye (jaise [0,1]),
    // to length = i - (-1) = i + 1 aani chahiye. Ye entry na ho to wo miss ho jayega.
    mpp[0] = -1;

    int maxlen = 0;   // ab tak ki sabse lambi balanced subarray

    for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {

        // Transformation: 0 -> -1, 1 -> +1
        if (nums[i] == 0) cumsum -= 1;
        else cumsum += 1;

        // Ye balance pehle aa chuka hai?
        if (mpp.find(cumsum) != mpp.end()) {
            // Haan: pehle index se ab tak ka hissa balanced hai.
            // Length = current index - pehli baar dikhne wala index.
            // Map update NAHI karte, kyunki hume LONGEST chahiye.
            // Pehla (sabse purana) index rakhne se length sabse badi milti hai.
            // Agar index badal dete, to length chhoti ho jati.
            maxlen = max(maxlen, i - mpp[cumsum]);
        }
        else {
            // Nahi: ye balance pehli baar dikha, to iska index save kar lo.
            mpp[cumsum] = i;
        }
    }

    return maxlen;
}

// Time: O(n)  (ek pass)
// Space: O(n) (worst case har balance alag ho)
//
// 560 se farq:
// 560 mein COUNT chahiye tha, to har baar mpp[sum]++ (frequency).
// 525 mein LONGEST chahiye, to sirf pehla index store hota hai aur kabhi overwrite nahi hota.


Transformation kab sochni hai (pehchaan ke signals)
1. "Equal number of A and B" → A ko +1, B ko -1, target 0.
2. "More A than B" / majority / strictly greater → +1/-1 aur sum > 0.
3. "Count of elements with property P" (odd, divisible, greater than x) → P wale ko 1, baaki ko 0, phir ye "sum = k" wala 560 ban jata hai.
4. "Even / odd frequency", "palindrome ban sakta hai", "at most one odd" → har character ke liye bit, aur prefix XOR mask.
5. "Divisible by k" → prefix sum ka remainder store karo.
6. Kisi fixed value (median, pivot) se compare → bada +1, chhota -1.




LC 930 (sliding window and prefix sum two approach) 

Method 1: Prefix Sum + HashMap (exactly goal)

Steps:

sum = running prefix sum, mpp = prefix sum kitni baar aaya (frequency).
mpp[0]++ se shuru karo (empty prefix), taaki shuru se hi goal ke barabar wali subarray miss na ho.
Har element pe sum += nums[i].
diff = sum - goal nikalo. Agar pehle koi prefix diff ke barabar tha, to uske baad se ab tak ki subarray ka sum exactly goal hai.
cnt += mpp[diff], kyunki diff kai baar aa chuka ho sakta hai aur har baar ek alag subarray banti hai.
Uske baad mpp[sum]++ (pehle check, phir insert).

Ye bilkul 560 ka code hai.

Method 2: Sliding Window, atMost(goal) - atMost(goal-1)

Idea: “Exactly goal” ko seedha sliding window se nahi pakad sakte. Lekin “at most goal” pakad sakte hain. To:

exactly(goal) = atMost(goal) - atMost(goal-1)

Matlab jin subarrays ka sum ≤ goal hai, unmein se wo hata do jinka sum ≤ goal-1 hai. Bachte hain sirf sum = goal wale.

func(nums, goal) ke steps (count of subarrays with sum ≤ goal):

goal < 0 ho to 0 return karo. Ye goal = 0 pe zaroori hai, kyunki tab func(goal-1) ko -1 milega.
Do pointers l, r = 0, sum = 0.
r ko aage badhao, sum += nums[r].
Agar sum > goal, to l ko aage badhao aur sum -= nums[l] karo, jab tak sum <= goal na ho jaye.
Ab [l..r] valid window hai. r pe end hone wali valid subarrays l, l+1, ..., r se shuru ho sakti hain, yaani r - l + 1. Ye cnt mein add karo.
r++ karke repeat.

Main function: func(goal) - func(goal-1).

Example: nums = [1,0,1,0,1], goal = 2. atMost(2) = 14, atMost(1) = 10, answer = 4. ✓

Dono mein farq
	HashMap	Sliding Window
Time	O(n)	O(n), lekin 2 pass
Space	O(n)	O(1)
Negative numbers	Chalta hai	Nahi chalta
Kab chalega	Hamesha	Sirf jab elements ≥ 0 hon (monotonic sum)

930 mein array binary hai (0/1), isliye dono chalte hain. 560 mein negatives ho sakte hain, isliye wahan sirf HashMap chalta hai.

Ek improvement: tumhare func(vector<int> nums, ...) mein vector copy hota hai. const vector<int>& nums likho, warna har call pe O(n) extra copy lagegi.

Yaad rakhne ka trick:

HashMap: “sum - goal pehle dikha?”
Window: “atMost(goal) - atMost(goal-1), aur har r pe r - l + 1 add karo.”
